SOAPBOX: It was the 5th CQ 160m contest since the 160m SSB was lifted
SOAPBOX: in Japan.
SOAPBOX: The Japanese SSB band has a width of only 30KHz from 1845 to
SOAPBOX: 1875KHz.
SOAPBOX: Please attention, JA stations can tranmit on 1848kHz low edge.
SOAPBOX: In Europe and the United States, band plans are not laws and
SOAPBOX: there are no penalties, but in Japan they are legal, so if we
SOAPBOX: do not follow the band plan, we will be sentenced to
SOAPBOX: imprisonment or a fine at worst.
SOAPBOX: During the CQ160m contest, in Europe and the United States,
SOAPBOX: the entire 160m band is almost filled with SSB, regardless of
SOAPBOX: the band plan, regardless of the band plan.
SOAPBOX: However, from Japan, only about half of these operating Western
SOAPBOX: countries are in the Japanese SSB band, so it is not possible
SOAPBOX: to call more than half of the stations.
SOAPBOX: Western stations sometimes watch the Japanese SSB band (1848-1875KHz).
SOAPBOX: My antenna is a Micro Vert it's length is only 4meters and 15meters
SOAPBOX: high from ground. It has a only one radial which length a only
SOAPBOX: 30meters length.
